   :control "Strategic-mode inference reads its six required features through the observation envelope and returns a typed record; no feature is read through a 0.0 default. :present carries the classified :mode and the six finite :features it rests on. :unknown means a REQUIRED FEATURE WAS NOT OBSERVED -- :mode is :unknown, no classification is offered, and :absent names every missing feature with the envelope's own reason and paths. Six absences previously arrived as six zeros and could fabricate :dark (the branch an EMPTY scan reached), suppress :depositing, or help satisfy :hermit. :refused means a feature was present but not a finite number, with :offending naming each one; a refusal still carries :absent, so neither fault is lost. There is NO partial or prior rule -- the classifier's :else branch asserts all six conditions failed, so one absent feature makes the whole classification unsupported. Whether anything may ACT on :unknown is the separate hard-guard decision (DECISIONS-PENDING 3) and is untouched. Code: src/futon2/aif/free_energy.clj:291-436 (features :300-311, classifier :313-347, producer :349-423, keyword form :425-436); caller scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj:4687-4701 takes :mode from the record; the record persists present-only at src/futon2/aif/trace.clj:547-554."
